    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1353" root="انس" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانٌ مَأْنُوسٌ</span></b> , (M,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَلٌّ مَأْنُوسٌ</span>, (A,) [<i>A
place,</i> and] <i>a place of alighting</i> or <i>abode, in which
is</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُنْس</span> [i. e. <i>sociableness,</i> &amp;c.]: (A:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مأنوس</span> is a
kind of possessive noun, because they did not say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَسْتُ المَكَانَ</span>, nor <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنِسْتُهُ</span>. (M, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَأْنُوسَةُ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَأْنُوسَةُ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنِيسٌ</span>.

